From e413449836e37d6014493c2c73b811adc38c80ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shima sheibani <shima.sheibani72@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 10:27:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fix context load failure: remove nonexistent MySQL8Dialect
 reference

Hibernate 7.2.7 (used by Spring Boot 4.0.5) no longer ships
org.hibernate.dialect.MySQL8Dialect - version-specific MySQL dialects
were consolidated into a single auto-detecting org.hibernate.dialect.MySQLDialect.
The hardcoded reference caused ClassNotFoundException when building the
EntityManagerFactory, failing ApplicationContext startup.

Removed the explicit dialect property entirely; Hibernate auto-detects
the correct dialect from the JDBC connection metadata, which is the
modern recommended approach and avoids hardcoding a class name that can
change between Hibernate versions.
---
 tms/src/main/resources/application.properties | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tms/src/main/resources/application.properties b/tms/src/main/resources/application.properties
index 0e3d05d..8cc3217 100644
--- a/tms/src/main/resources/application.properties
+++ b/tms/src/main/resources/application.properties
@@ -5,7 +5,6 @@ spring.datasource.password=${DB_PASSWORD}
 spring.datasource.driver-class-name=com.mysql.cj.jdbc.Driver
 spring.jpa.hibernate.ddl-auto=update
 spring.jpa.show-sql=true
-spring.jpa.properties.hibernate.dialect=org.hibernate.dialect.MySQL8Dialect
 
 
 
